# Linux RAM Full Troubleshooting Lab

## Project Overview
This lab simulates a Linux server running out of RAM memory and demonstrates basic troubleshooting steps used in IT Support and Cloud Support roles.

## Scenario
A Linux system becomes slow because RAM usage reaches 100%.

Goal:
- Identify high memory usage
- Investigate running processes
- Clear memory usage
- Restore normal system performance

---

## Environment
- OS: Ubuntu 22.04
- Virtual Machine: VirtualBox
- RAM Assigned: 2 GB

---

## Step 1: Check Memory Usage

Commands used:

```bash
free -h
top
htop

Step 2: Simulate RAM Full Condition

Used the following command to consume memory:

stress --vm 2 --vm-bytes 1G --timeout 120s

Step 3: Identify High Memory Process

Commands:

top
ps aux --sort=-%mem | head

Observed high memory consumption from stress process.
Step 4: Troubleshooting Steps

Stopped the memory-consuming process:

kill -9 <PID>

Verified memory recovery:

free -h
